### A book's own accessibility information (EPUB Accessibility metadata).

## Said after the document overview and printed by tw info for an EPUB,
## one fact per line, meaning first. The first line is one of the four
## leads; the details follow when the book gives them. $list is a list of
## terms in words ("table of contents, alternative text"), $text the
## publisher's own words, $name a certifier's name.
access-info-friendly = Accessibility: screen reader friendly, per the publisher.
access-info-not-text = Accessibility: not all of it reads as text, per the publisher.
access-info-given = Accessibility: described by the publisher.
access-info-none = No accessibility information given.
access-info-summary = Summary: { $text }.
access-info-modes = Access modes: { $list }.
access-info-sufficient = Readable with: { $list }.
access-info-features = Features: { $list }.
access-info-hazards = Hazards: { $list }.
access-info-conformance = Conforms to: { $text }.
access-info-certifier = Certified by: { $name }.
# Joins two sets of access modes in access-info-sufficient: "text, or text and images".
access-info-or = { $first }, or { $second }
# Joins the access modes inside one set: "text and images".
access-info-and = { $first } and { $second }
